// Test: bugfixes/any_unknown_method_is_func001
// Grammar: method_call
// Semantic: FUNC001 — a method an `any` value does not have is an error, not a call to an unrelated function
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.176
// Expected output:
// Expected error:
//   FUNC001
//   Method 'toUpperCase' not found on an `any` value
//
// Regression: a method on an `any` other than the ones the compiler lowers
// (`toString`, `toInteger`, `toNumber`, `toBoolean`, `length`, `get`,
// `isDefined`, `isNotDefined`, `isEmpty`, `isNotEmpty`) compiled to a call
// of the print function: `name.toUpperCase()` printed the value and
// returned garbage.

start:
	any data = json.textToData("{\"name\": \"abc\"}")
	any name = data.name
	any upper = name.toUpperCase()
	printl(upper.toString())
